    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0271" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg237"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 30, of the
                    13th ultimo, I have the honor to inform you that I have now been officially
                    notified by the German foreign office that Jonas Lippmann has been recognized by
                    the authorities of Alsace-Lorraine as an American citizen, and the sentence
                    passed in his case on March 3, 1888, on account of his not presenting himself
                    for military duty, has been revoked, and his name taken from the list of those
                    liable to be called upon for service in the army.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">And. D. White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
